  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Periodic chances for showers and storms will \ncontinue toward the western Southern Tier through midweek, with \nmainly dry weather expected for the remainder of western and north-\ncentral NY.\n\nA cold front sagging slowly southward across the area early this \nmorning will settle somewhere just south of the NY/PA state line by \nlate morning/midday. This will serve as the focal point for periodic \nshowers and thunderstorms as ill-timed convectively augmented \nshortwaves/ridge riders travel southeast along or near this \nboundary. Due to the close proximity of the stalled boundary to the \nwestern Southern Tier, it is expected that this area may at least be \ngrazed by the northern periphery of these systems as they slide by \njust to the south, bringing the potential for periodic rounds of \nshowers and storms through midweek. Otherwise, aside from a few \nshowers/storms from the Genesee Valley westward this morning, drier \nair residing to the north of the stalled front over northern PA is \nexpected to provide mainly dry weather for the remainder of our area \nthrough at least midday Wednesday before the next system within a \npersistent northwesterly flow regime approaches from the northwest \nbringing the next chance for a few showers/storms by Wednesday \nafternoon. \n\nThe passage of the cold front will bring little change in our \ntemperatures through midweek, with highs right about where they \nshould be as we head toward the middle of August. However, there \nwill be a noticeable drop in humidity levels, making it feel more \ncomfortable.",
